[LineDescription "Pawn on the 2nd or 3rd rank: the key squares are two ranks in front. The king goes first."]

{[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5] For a pawn on the 2nd or 3rd rank the key squares are still
two ranks ahead of the pawn. The pawn does not need to move at all yet: bring
the king up first. Pawn on d3: the key squares (green) are c5, d5, e5.} 1. Kd2
Kb4 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 2. Ke3 Kc5 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 3. Ke4 Kd6 {[%csl
Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 4. Kd4 {Opposition! The kings face each other with one square
between them, and Black must give way.} 4... Kc6 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 5. Ke5
{Key square e5! With your king here the pawn will queen, whoever is to move. Now
escort it all the way.} 5... Kd7 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 6. Kd5 {Opposition again.}
6... Kc7 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 7. Ke6 {The king walks ahead of the pawn and
clears the way; the pawn follows.} 7... Kb6 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 8. d4 {Now the
pawn advances, with the king clearing the way.} 8... Kc7 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6]} 9.
d5 {Pawn forward.} 9... Kd8 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 10. Kd6 {Opposition
again.} 10... Kc8 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 11. Ke7 Kc7 {[%csl
Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 12. d6+ {Pawn forward, with check.} 12... Kc6 {[%csl
Gc7,Gd7,Ge7,Gc8,Gd8,Ge8]} 13. d7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king
guards the queening square: nothing can stop it now.} 13... Kc7 {[%csl Gd8]} 14.
d8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king is
an easy win.} *

