Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 4. Kd6 {Opposition! The kings face each other with one
square between them, and Black must give way.} 4... Kc8 {[%csl
Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 5. Ke7 {The king walks ahead of the pawn and clears
the way; the pawn follows.} 5... Kc7 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 6. d6+
{Now the pawn advances, with the king clearing the way.} 6... Kc6 {[%csl
Gc7,Gd7,Ge7,Gc8,Gd8,Ge8]} 7. d7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king
guards the queening square: nothing can stop it now.} 7... Kc7 {[%csl Gd8]} 8.
d8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king is
an easy win.} *

