{[%csl Gc7,Gd7,Ge7,Gc8,Gd8,Ge8] A pawn on the 6th rank with your king beside it
wins against any defence. Watch how king and pawn work together all the way to
the queening square. Pawn on d6: the key squares (green) are c7, d7, e7, c8, d8,
e8.} 1. Kc6 {Opposition! The kings face each other with one square between them,
and Black must give way.} 1... Kd8 {[%csl Gc7,Gd7,Ge7,Gc8,Gd8,Ge8]} 2. d7 {Now
the pawn advances, with the king clearing the way.} 2... Ke7 {[%csl Gd8]} 3. Kc7
{Opposition again.} 3... Ke6 {[%csl Gd8]} 4. d8=Q {Queen! The pawn has promoted
safely, and king and queen against king is an easy win.} *

