[Event "05. The opposition (1/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/1k6/8/8/1K1P4/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "05. The opposition (1/5)"]
[LineDescription "Opposition: kings face to face, one square apart, and the opponent has to move."]

{[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4] Rule 2: when the kings stand on the same file with ONE
square between them, the side that does NOT have to move has the OPPOSITION. The
other king must step aside and let yours through. Take the opposition, then walk
forward to a key square. Pawn on d2: the key squares (green) are c4, d4, e4.} 1.
Kb3 {Opposition! The kings face each other with one square between them, and
Black must give way.} 1... Kc5 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 2. Kc3 {Opposition again.}
2... Kd5 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 3. Kd3 {Opposition again.} 3... Kc5 {[%csl
Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 4. Ke4 {Key square e4! With your king here the pawn will queen,
whoever is to move. Now escort it all the way.} 4... Kd6 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 5.
Kd4 {Opposition again.} 5... Kc6 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 6. Ke5 {The king walks
ahead of the pawn and clears the way; the pawn follows.} 6... Kd7 {[%csl
Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 7. Kd5 {[%also d3] Opposition again.} 7... Kc7 {[%csl
Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 8. Ke6 {[%also d3]} 8... Kb6 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 9. d4 {Now the
pawn advances, with the king clearing the way.} 9... Kc7 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6]}
10. d5 {Pawn forward.} 10... Kd8 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 11. Kd6
{Opposition again.} 11... Kc8 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 12. Ke7 Kc7
{[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 13. d6+ {Pawn forward, with check.} 13... Kc6
{[%csl Gc7,Gd7,Ge7,Gc8,Gd8,Ge8]} 14. d7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your
king guards the queening square: nothing can stop it now.} 14... Kc7 {[%csl
Gd8]} 15. d8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against
king is an easy win.} *

