[LineName "05. The opposition (2/5)"]
[LineDescription "Opposition: kings face to face, one square apart, and the opponent has to move."]

{[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4] Take the opposition, then march to a key square. Pawn on e2:
the key squares (green) are d4, e4, f4.} 1. Kg3 {Opposition! The kings face each
other with one square between them, and Black must give way.} 1... Kf5 {[%csl
Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 2. Kf3 {Opposition again.} 2... Ke5 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 3. Ke3
{Opposition again.} 3... Kd5 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 4. Kf4 {Key square f4! With
your king here the pawn will queen, whoever is to move. Now escort it all the
way.} 4... Ke6 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 5. Ke4 {Opposition again.} 5... Kd6 {[%csl
Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 6. Kf5 {The king walks ahead of the pawn and clears the way; the
pawn follows.} 6... Ke7 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 7. Ke5 {[%also e3] Opposition
again.} 7... Kd7 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 8. Kf6 {[%also e3]} 8... Kc6 {[%csl
Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 9. e4 {Now the pawn advances, with the king clearing the way.}
9... Kd7 {[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6]} 10. e5 {Pawn forward.} 10... Ke8 {[%csl
Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 11. Ke6 {Opposition again.} 11... Kd8 {[%csl
Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 12. Kf7 Kd7 {[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 13. e6+
{Pawn forward, with check.} 13... Kd6 {[%csl Gd7,Ge7,Gf7,Gd8,Ge8,Gf8]} 14. e7
{The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king guards the queening square: nothing
can stop it now.} 14... Kd7 {[%csl Ge8]} 15. e8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted
safely, and king and queen against king is an easy win.} *

