[LineName "06. With the opposition, Black must give way (1/3)"]
[LineDescription "When the defender gives way, step past him on the side he left."]

{Here you already have the opposition and it is Black to move. Whichever way
Black steps, your king walks past on the side he has just left open. Pawn on d2:
the key squares (green) are c4, d4, e4. Black moves first.} 1... Kc6 {[%csl
Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 2. Kc4 {Key square c4! With your king here the pawn will queen,
whoever is to move. Now escort it all the way.} 2... Kd6 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 3.
Kd4 {Opposition! The kings face each other with one square between them, and
Black must give way.} 3... Kc6 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 4. Ke5 {The king walks ahead
of the pawn and clears the way; the pawn follows.} 4... Kd7 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]}
5. Kd5 {[%also d3] Opposition again.} 5... Kc7 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 6. Ke6
{[%also d3]} 6... Kb6 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 7. d4 {Now the pawn advances, with
the king clearing the way.} 7... Kc7 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6]} 8. d5 {Pawn forward.}
8... Kd8 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 9. Kd6 {Opposition again.} 9... Kc8
{[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 10. Ke7 Kc7 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]}
11. d6+ {Pawn forward, with check.} 11... Kc6 {[%csl Gc7,Gd7,Ge7,Gc8,Gd8,Ge8]}
12. d7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king guards the queening square:
nothing can stop it now.} 12... Kc7 {[%csl Gd8]} 13. d8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has
promoted safely, and king and queen against king is an easy win.} *

