[Event "07. Distant opposition (1/2)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "1k6/8/8/8/8/K2P4/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "07. Distant opposition (1/2)"]
[LineDescription "Distant opposition: same file, an odd number of squares between the kings."]

{[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5] Opposition also works from far away: the same file with
three (or five) squares between the kings. Take it at a distance and it turns
into the direct opposition as the kings come closer. Pawn on d3: the key squares
(green) are c5, d5, e5.} 1. Kb4 {Distant opposition: same file, three squares
apart. Keep it and it becomes the direct opposition.} 1... Kc7 {[%csl
Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 2. Kc5 {Key square c5! With your king here the pawn will queen,
whoever is to move. Now escort it all the way.} 2... Kd7 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 3.
Kd5 {Opposition! The kings face each other with one square between them, and
Black must give way.} 3... Kc7 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 4. Ke6 {The king walks ahead
of the pawn and clears the way; the pawn follows.} 4... Kb6 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]}
5. d4 {Now the pawn advances, with the king clearing the way.} 5... Kc7 {[%csl
Gc6,Gd6,Ge6]} 6. d5 {Pawn forward.} 6... Kd8 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 7.
Kd6 {Opposition again.} 7... Kc8 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 8. Ke7 Kc7
{[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 9. d6+ {Pawn forward, with check.} 9... Kc6
{[%csl Gc7,Gd7,Ge7,Gc8,Gd8,Ge8]} 10. d7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your
king guards the queening square: nothing can stop it now.} 10... Kc7 {[%csl
Gd8]} 11. d8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against
king is an easy win.} *

