[Event "08. Diagonal opposition (1/2)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/5k2/8/8/3KP3/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "08. Diagonal opposition (1/2)"]
[LineDescription "Diagonal opposition turns into direct opposition or a key square."]

{[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6] Kings on the same diagonal with one square between them are
also in opposition. Use it to shadow the defending king and step onto a key
square. Pawn on e4: the key squares (green) are d6, e6, f6.} 1. Kd5 {Diagonal
opposition: next move it turns into a key square or the direct opposition.} 1...
Kf6 {[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6]} 2. Kd6 {Key square d6! With your king here the pawn
will queen, whoever is to move. Now escort it all the way.} 2... Kf7 {[%csl
Gd6,Ge6,Gf6]} 3. e5 {Now the pawn advances, with the king clearing the way.}
3... Ke8 {[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 4. Ke6 {Opposition! The kings face
each other with one square between them, and Black must give way.} 4... Kd8
{[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 5. Kf7 {The king walks ahead of the pawn and
clears the way; the pawn follows.} 5... Kd7 {[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 6.
e6+ {Pawn forward, with check.} 6... Kd6 {[%csl Gd7,Ge7,Gf7,Gd8,Ge8,Gf8]} 7. e7
{The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king guards the queening square: nothing
can stop it now.} 7... Kd7 {[%csl Ge8]} 8. e8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted
safely, and king and queen against king is an easy win.} *

