[Event "09. King first, pawn later (1/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/8/1k6/3P4/3K4 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "09. King first, pawn later (1/4)"]
[LineDescription "Lead with the king; the pawn follows later."]

{[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4] The most common mistake in these endings is pushing the pawn
too early. A pawn that runs ahead of its king gives the defender time to block
it. Bring the king in front first, and only then push. Pawn on d2: the key
squares (green) are c4, d4, e4.} 1. Ke2 {(d3 would only draw: king first, pawn
later.)} 1... Kc4 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 2. Ke3 Kd5 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 3. Kd3
{Opposition! The kings face each other with one square between them, and Black
must give way.} 3... Kc5 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 4. Ke4 {Key square e4! With your
king here the pawn will queen, whoever is to move. Now escort it all the way.}
4... Kd6 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 5. Kd4 {Opposition again.} 5... Kc6 {[%csl
Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 6. Ke5 {The king walks ahead of the pawn and clears the way; the
pawn follows.} 6... Kd7 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 7. Kd5 {[%also d3] Opposition
again.} 7... Kc7 {[%csl Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 8. Ke6 {[%also d3]} 8... Kb6 {[%csl
Gc4,Gd4,Ge4]} 9. d4 {Now the pawn advances, with the king clearing the way.}
9... Kc7 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6]} 10. d5 {Pawn forward.} 10... Kd8 {[%csl
Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 11. Kd6 {Opposition again.} 11... Kc8 {[%csl
Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 12. Ke7 Kc7 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 13. d6+
{Pawn forward, with check.} 13... Kc6 {[%csl Gc7,Gd7,Ge7,Gc8,Gd8,Ge8]} 14. d7
{The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king guards the queening square: nothing
can stop it now.} 14... Kc7 {[%csl Gd8]} 15. d8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted
safely, and king and queen against king is an easy win.} *

[Event "09. King first, pawn later (2/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/8/6k1/4P3/4K3 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "09. King first, pawn later (2/4)"]
[LineDescription "Lead with the king; the pawn follows later."]

{[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4] Resist the pawn move. King first! Pawn on e2: the key
squares (green) are d4, e4, f4.} 1. Kd2 {(e3 would only draw: king first, pawn
later.)} 1... Kf4 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 2. Kd3 Ke5 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 3. Ke3
{Opposition! The kings face each other with one square between them, and Black
must give way.} 3... Kd5 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 4. Kf4 {Key square f4! With your
king here the pawn will queen, whoever is to move. Now escort it all the way.}
4... Ke6 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 5. Ke4 {Opposition again.} 5... Kd6 {[%csl
Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 6. Kf5 {The king walks ahead of the pawn and clears the way; the
pawn follows.} 6... Ke7 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 7. Ke5 {[%also e3] Opposition
again.} 7... Kd7 {[%csl Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 8. Kf6 {[%also e3]} 8... Kc6 {[%csl
Gd4,Ge4,Gf4]} 9. e4 {Now the pawn advances, with the king clearing the way.}
9... Kd7 {[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6]} 10. e5 {Pawn forward.} 10... Ke8 {[%csl
Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 11. Ke6 {Opposition again.} 11... Kd8 {[%csl
Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 12. Kf7 Kd7 {[%csl Gd6,Ge6,Gf6,Gd7,Ge7,Gf7]} 13. e6+
{Pawn forward, with check.} 13... Kd6 {[%csl Gd7,Ge7,Gf7,Gd8,Ge8,Gf8]} 14. e7
{The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king guards the queening square: nothing
can stop it now.} 14... Kd7 {[%csl Ge8]} 15. e8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted
safely, and king and queen against king is an easy win.} *

[Event "09. King first, pawn later (3/4)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/1k6/8/3P4/3K4/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "09. King first, pawn later (3/4)"]
[LineDescription "Lead with the king; the pawn follows later."]

{[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5] Resist the pawn move. King first! Pawn on d3: the key
squares (green) are c5, d5, e5.} 1. Ke3 {(d4 would only draw: king first, pawn
later.)} 1... Kc5 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 2. Ke4 Kd6 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 3. Kd4
{Opposition! The kings face each other with one square between them, and Black
must give way.} 3... Kc6 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 4. Ke5 {Key square e5! With your
king here the pawn will queen, whoever is to move. Now escort it all the way.}
4... Kd7 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 5. Kd5 {Opposition again.} 5... Kc7 {[%csl
Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 6. Ke6 {The king walks ahead of the pawn and clears the way; the
pawn follows.} 6... Kb6 {[%csl Gc5,Gd5,Ge5]} 7. d4 {Now the pawn advances, with
the king clearing the way.} 7... Kc7 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6]} 8. d5 {Pawn forward.}
8... Kd8 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 9. Kd6 {Opposition again.} 9... Kc8
{[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]} 10. Ke7 Kc7 {[%csl Gc6,Gd6,Ge6,Gc7,Gd7,Ge7]}
11. d6+ {Pawn forward, with check.} 11... Kc6 {[%csl Gc7,Gd7,Ge7,Gc8,Gd8,Ge8]}
12. d7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king guards the queening square:
nothing can stop it now.} 12... Kc7 {[%csl Gd8]} 13. d8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has
promoted safely, and king and queen against king is an easy win.} *

