[Event "10. Defending: keep the opposition (1/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/3p4/2k5/8/1K6/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "10. Defending: keep the opposition (1/5)"]
[LineDescription "Defender's rule: stay in front of the pawn and keep the opposition."]

{[%csl Rc5,Rd5,Re5] Now YOU defend: Black has the pawn. If you keep the
opposition in front of the pawn, the black king can never reach a key square and
the game is a draw. Black's pawn is on d7. You are White: hold the draw. Red
squares: the key squares Black's king must never reach.} 1. Kc4 {Opposition!
Black's king cannot advance.} 1... Kd6 {[%csl Rc5,Rd5,Re5]} 2. Kd4 {Opposition
again.} 2... Kc6 {[%csl Rc5,Rd5,Re5]} 3. Kc4 {Opposition again.} 3... d6 {[%csl
Rc4,Rd4,Re4] Black pushes. Keep your king in front of the pawn.} 4. Kd4 Kb5
{[%csl Rc4,Rd4,Re4]} 5. Kd5 {[%also Kd3] Opposition again.} 5... Kb4 {[%csl
Rc4,Rd4,Re4]} 6. Kxd6 {You win the pawn: draw!} *

[Event "10. Defending: keep the opposition (2/5)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
