[LineName "10. Defending: keep the opposition (2/5)"]
[LineDescription "Defender's rule: stay in front of the pawn and keep the opposition."]

{[%csl Rd5,Re5,Rf5] Hold the opposition and Black gets nowhere. Black's pawn is
on e7. You are White: hold the draw. Red squares: the key squares Black's king
must never reach.} 1. Kd4 {Opposition! Black's king cannot advance.} 1... Ke6
{[%csl Rd5,Re5,Rf5]} 2. Ke4 {Opposition again.} 2... Kf6 {[%csl Rd5,Re5,Rf5]} 3.
Kf4 {Opposition again.} 3... Ke6 {[%csl Rd5,Re5,Rf5]} 4. Ke4 {Opposition again.}
4... Kd7 {[%csl Rd5,Re5,Rf5]} 5. Kd5 {[%also Kd3,Ke3,Ke5] Opposition again.}
5... Ke8 {[%csl Rd5,Re5,Rf5]} 6. Ke6 {[%also Kd4,Ke4,Ke5] Opposition again.}
6... Kd8 {[%csl Rd5,Re5,Rf5]} 7. Kd5 {[%also Ke5,Kf5]} 7... Kd7 {[%csl
Rd5,Re5,Rf5]} 8. Ke5 Kc6 {[%csl Rd5,Re5,Rf5]} 9. Ke6 {[%also Ke4] Opposition
again.} 9... Kc5 {[%csl Rd5,Re5,Rf5]} 10. Kxe7 {You win the pawn: draw!} *

