[Event "11. Defending: retreat straight back (1/3)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/4k3/3p4/3K4/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "11. Defending: retreat straight back (1/3)"]
[LineDescription "Retreat straight back, so you can take the opposition when the pawn moves."]

{[%csl Rc2,Rd2,Re2,Rc1,Rd1,Re1] When you have to retreat, go STRAIGHT BACK in
front of the pawn, never to the side. Then, as soon as the pawn advances, you
can take the opposition again. Black's pawn is on d3. You are White: hold the
draw. Red squares: the key squares Black's king must never reach.} 1. Kd1
{Straight back, in front of the pawn. Now you can take the opposition after the
pawn moves.} 1... Kf3 {[%csl Rc2,Rd2,Re2,Rc1,Rd1,Re1]} 2. Kd2 Kf4 {[%csl
Rc2,Rd2,Re2,Rc1,Rd1,Re1]} 3. Kxd3 {You win the pawn: draw!} *

