[Event "12. Defending: the stalemate trap (1/2)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/8/2k5/3pK3/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "12. Defending: the stalemate trap (1/2)"]
[LineDescription "Blocking the queening square often ends in stalemate."]

{[%csl Gd1] With the pawn already on the 2nd rank, step in front of it. If Black
protects the pawn, it is stalemate! Black's pawn is on d2. You are White: hold
the draw. Green: the queening square you must block.} 1. Kd1 {Step in front of
the pawn: the queening square is blocked.} 1... Kd3 {[%csl Gd1] Stalemate! White
has no legal move: the game is drawn.} *

[Event "12. Defending: the stalemate trap (2/2)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/8/5k2/3Kp3/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "12. Defending: the stalemate trap (2/2)"]
[LineDescription "Blocking the queening square often ends in stalemate."]

{[%csl Ge1] Block the queening square and look for stalemate. Black's pawn is on
e2. You are White: hold the draw. Green: the queening square you must block.} 1.
Ke1 {Step in front of the pawn: the queening square is blocked.} 1... Ke3 {[%csl
Ge1] Stalemate! White has no legal move: the game is drawn.} *

[Event "13. Rook pawn: the key square next to the corner (1/3)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/3k4/PK6/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "13. Rook pawn: the key square next to the corner (1/3)"]
[LineDescription "Rook pawn: the key squares are b7/b8 (a-pawn) or g7/g8 (h-pawn)."]

{[%csl Gb7,Gb8] Rook pawns are special: the defender draws if his king reaches
the corner in front of the pawn. To win, your king must reach the key square
next to the queening corner (b7/b8 for an a-pawn, g7/g8 for an h-pawn). Pawn on
a4: the key squares (green) are b7, b8.} 1. Kb5 {Opposition! The kings face each
other with one square between them, and Black must give way.} 1... Kd6 {[%csl
Gb7,Gb8]} 2. Kb6 {Opposition again.} 2... Kd7 {[%csl Gb7,Gb8]} 3. Kb7 {Key
square b7! With your king here the pawn will queen, whoever is to move. Now
escort it all the way.} 3... Kd6 {[%csl Gb7,Gb8]} 4. a5 {Now the pawn advances,
with the king clearing the way.} 4... Kc5 {[%csl Gb7,Gb8]} 5. a6 {Pawn forward.}
5... Kb5 {[%csl Gb7,Gb8]} 6. a7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king
guards the queening square: nothing can stop it now.} 6... Ka5 {[%csl Gb7,Gb8]}
7. a8=Q+ {Queen! The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king
is an easy win.} *

[Event "13. Rook pawn: the key square next to the corner (2/3)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/4k3/6KP/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "13. Rook pawn: the key square next to the corner (2/3)"]
[LineDescription "Rook pawn: the key squares are b7/b8 (a-pawn) or g7/g8 (h-pawn)."]

{[%csl Gg7,Gg8] Head for the key square beside the corner. Pawn on h4: the key
squares (green) are g7, g8.} 1. Kg5 {Opposition! The kings face each other with
one square between them, and Black must give way.} 1... Ke6 {[%csl Gg7,Gg8]} 2.
Kg6 {Opposition again.} 2... Ke7 {[%csl Gg7,Gg8]} 3. Kg7 {Key square g7! With
your king here the pawn will queen, whoever is to move. Now escort it all the
way.} 3... Ke6 {[%csl Gg7,Gg8]} 4. h5 {Now the pawn advances, with the king
clearing the way.} 4... Kf5 {[%csl Gg7,Gg8]} 5. h6 {Pawn forward.} 5... Kg5
{[%csl Gg7,Gg8]} 6. h7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king guards the
queening square: nothing can stop it now.} 6... Kf5 {[%csl Gg7,Gg8]} 7. h8=Q
{Queen! The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king is an easy
win.} *

[Event "13. Rook pawn: the key square next to the corner (3/3)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/K7/8/Pk6/8/8/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "13. Rook pawn: the key square next to the corner (3/3)"]
[LineDescription "Rook pawn: the key squares are b7/b8 (a-pawn) or g7/g8 (h-pawn)."]

{[%csl Gb7,Gb8] Head for the key square beside the corner. Pawn on a5: the key
squares (green) are b7, b8.} 1. a6 {Now the pawn advances, with the king
clearing the way.} 1... Ka5 {[%csl Gb7,Gb8] Black takes the opposition, so you
go around him: outflanking.} 2. Kb7 {Key square b7! With your king here the pawn
will queen, whoever is to move. Now escort it all the way.} 2... Kb5 {[%csl
Gb7,Gb8]} 3. a7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king guards the queening
square: nothing can stop it now.} 3... Ka5 {[%csl Gb7,Gb8]} 4. a8=Q+ {Queen! The
pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king is an easy win.} *

[Event "14. Rook pawn: run to the corner (1/3)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/7p/6k1/3K4/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "14. Rook pawn: run to the corner (1/3)"]
[LineDescription "Against a rook pawn, the corner in front of it is a fortress."]

{[%csl Gh1,Gg1] Defending against a rook pawn: get your king to the corner in
front of it. From there it can never be driven out, and Black can only stalemate
you. Black's pawn is on h5. You are White: hold the draw. Green: the corner
squares your king is heading for.} 1. Ke2 {Towards the corner: against a rook
pawn, a king in the corner cannot be driven out.} 1... Kg3 {[%csl Gh1,Gg1]} 2.
Kf1 h4 {[%csl Gh1,Gg1] Black pushes. Keep your king in front of the pawn.} 3.
Kg1 {In the corner! Now Black can never drive you out.} 3... h3 {[%csl Gh1,Gg1]}
4. Kh1 h2 {[%csl Gh1,Gg1] Stalemate! White has no legal move: the game is
drawn.} *

[Event "14. Rook pawn: run to the corner (2/3)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/p7/2k5/4K3/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "14. Rook pawn: run to the corner (2/3)"]
[LineDescription "Against a rook pawn, the corner in front of it is a fortress."]

{[%csl Ga1,Gb1] Into the corner! Black's pawn is on a5. You are White: hold the
draw. Green: the corner squares your king is heading for.} 1. Kd2 {Towards the
corner: against a rook pawn, a king in the corner cannot be driven out.} 1...
Kb3 {[%csl Ga1,Gb1]} 2. Kc1 a4 {[%csl Ga1,Gb1] Black pushes. Keep your king in
front of the pawn.} 3. Kb1 {In the corner! Now Black can never drive you out.}
3... a3 {[%csl Ga1,Gb1]} 4. Ka1 a2 {[%csl Ga1,Gb1] Stalemate! White has no legal
move: the game is drawn.} *

[Event "14. Rook pawn: run to the corner (3/3)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/p1k5/4K3/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "14. Rook pawn: run to the corner (3/3)"]
[LineDescription "Against a rook pawn, the corner in front of it is a fortress."]

{[%csl Ga1,Gb1] Into the corner! Black's pawn is on a4. You are White: hold the
draw. Green: the corner squares your king is heading for.} 1. Kd2 {Towards the
corner: against a rook pawn, a king in the corner cannot be driven out.} 1...
Kb3 {[%csl Ga1,Gb1]} 2. Kc1 a3 {[%csl Ga1,Gb1] Black pushes. Keep your king in
front of the pawn.} 3. Kb1 {In the corner! Now Black can never drive you out.}
3... a2+ {[%csl Ga1,Gb1]} 4. Ka1 Ka3 {[%csl Ga1,Gb1] Stalemate! White has no
legal move: the game is drawn.} *

[Event "15. The rule of the square (1/3)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/4P3/3k4/8/K7 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "15. The rule of the square (1/3)"]
[LineDescription "Defending king outside the square: the pawn runs on its own."]

{[%csl Bb5,Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8,Be8] When the
kings are far apart, count! Imagine a square from the pawn to the queening rank.
If the enemy king is outside that square after your move, the pawn simply runs
and queens. The blue zone is the square of the pawn once it moves: if the black
king is outside it, the pawn queens.} 1. e5 {Run! After this push the black king
is outside the pawn's square.} 1... Kd4 {[%csl
Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bc7,Bd7,Be7,Bc8,Bd8,Be8]} 2. e6 {Keep running.} 2... Kd5 {[%csl
Bd7,Be7,Bd8,Be8]} 3. e7 {Keep running.} 3... Kd6 {[%csl Be8]} 4. e8=Q {Queen!
The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king is an easy win.} *

[Event "15. The rule of the square (2/3)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/3P4/2k5/8/7K w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "15. The rule of the square (2/3)"]
[LineDescription "Defending king outside the square: the pawn runs on its own."]

{[%csl Ba5,Bb5,Bc5,Bd5,Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Ba7,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Ba8,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8] Is the
king outside the square? Then run! The blue zone is the square of the pawn once
it moves: if the black king is outside it, the pawn queens.} 1. d5 {Run! After
this push the black king is outside the pawn's square.} 1... Kc4 {[%csl
Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Bb7,Bc7,Bd7,Bb8,Bc8,Bd8]} 2. d6 {Keep running.} 2... Kc5 {[%csl
Bc7,Bd7,Bc8,Bd8]} 3. d7 {Keep running.} 3... Kc6 {[%csl Bd8]} 4. d8=Q {Queen!
The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king is an easy win.} *

