[Event "16. Defending: catch the pawn (1/2)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/K4p2/8/8/1k6/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "16. Defending: catch the pawn (1/2)"]
[LineDescription "A king inside the square catches the pawn."]

{[%csl
Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Ba5,Bb5,Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Ba4,Bb4,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Ba3,Bb3,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Ba2,Bb2,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Ba1,Bb1,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1]
Now you are the one chasing. Step into the pawn's square and your king will
catch it in time. Black's pawn is on f6. You are White: hold the draw. Blue: the
pawn's square. Step into it.} 1. Kb5 {Into the pawn's square: your king will
catch it.} 1... Kc3 {[%csl
Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Ba5,Bb5,Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Ba4,Bb4,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Ba3,Bb3,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Ba2,Bb2,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Ba1,Bb1,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1]}
2. Kc5 {Opposition! Black's king cannot advance.} 2... Kd3 {[%csl
Ba6,Bb6,Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Ba5,Bb5,Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Ba4,Bb4,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Ba3,Bb3,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Ba2,Bb2,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Ba1,Bb1,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1]}
3. Kd5 {Opposition again.} 3... f5 {[%csl
Bb5,Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bb4,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Bb3,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bb2,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bb1,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1]
Black pushes. Keep your king in front of the pawn.} 4. Ke5 f4 {[%csl
Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1]} 5. Kxf4 {You
win the pawn: draw!} *

[Event "16. Defending: catch the pawn (2/2)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/2p4K/8/8/6k1/8/8 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "16. Defending: catch the pawn (2/2)"]
[LineDescription "A king inside the square catches the pawn."]

{[%csl
Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Bg4,Bh4,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bg3,Bh3,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bh2,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1,Bg1,Bh1]
Into the square, then catch the pawn. Black's pawn is on c6. You are White: hold
the draw. Blue: the pawn's square. Step into it.} 1. Kg5 {Into the pawn's
square: your king will catch it.} 1... Kf3 {[%csl
Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Bg4,Bh4,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bg3,Bh3,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bh2,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1,Bg1,Bh1]}
2. Kf5 {Opposition! Black's king cannot advance.} 2... Ke3 {[%csl
Bc6,Bd6,Be6,Bf6,Bg6,Bh6,Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bh5,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Bg4,Bh4,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bg3,Bh3,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bh2,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1,Bg1,Bh1]}
3. Ke5 {Opposition again.} 3... c5 {[%csl
Bc5,Bd5,Be5,Bf5,Bg5,Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Bg4,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bg3,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bg2,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1,Bg1]
Black pushes. Keep your king in front of the pawn.} 4. Kd5 c4 {[%csl
Bc4,Bd4,Be4,Bf4,Bc3,Bd3,Be3,Bf3,Bc2,Bd2,Be2,Bf2,Bc1,Bd1,Be1,Bf1]} 5. Kxc4 {You
win the pawn: draw!} *

[Event "17. Final exam (1/2)"]
[Site "Endgame Classroom"]
[White "?"]
[Black "?"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "8/8/8/8/8/2k1P3/8/3K4 w - - 0 1"]
[LineName "17. Final exam (1/2)"]
[LineDescription "Key squares + opposition = won king and pawn endings. Well done!"]

{Put it all together. Which squares are key? Who has the opposition? When should
the pawn move? Try this one in Practice mode without hints.} 1. Ke2 Kc4 2. Kf3
Kd5 3. Kf4 Ke6 4. Ke4 {Opposition! The kings face each other with one square
between them, and Black must give way.} 4... Kd6 5. Kf5 {Key square f5! With
your king here the pawn will queen, whoever is to move. Now escort it all the
way.} 5... Ke7 6. Ke5 {Opposition again.} 6... Kd7 7. Kf6 {The king walks ahead
of the pawn and clears the way; the pawn follows.} 7... Kc6 8. e4 {Now the pawn
advances, with the king clearing the way.} 8... Kd7 9. e5 {Pawn forward.} 9...
Ke8 10. Ke6 {Opposition again.} 10... Kd8 11. Kf7 Kd7 12. e6+ {Pawn forward,
with check.} 12... Kd6 13. e7 {The pawn reaches the 7th rank and your king
guards the queening square: nothing can stop it now.} 13... Kd7 14. e8=Q+
{Queen! The pawn has promoted safely, and king and queen against king is an easy
win.} *

